WEBVTT

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.020
Joonsang was...

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.790
He was my first love.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.090
How could I tell you that the reason I love you

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.430
is because you look like my dead first love?

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.660
Do you think you would have believed me if I said that?

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.760
Do you?

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.470
Then Miss Yujin,

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.520
as well as all your other friends, thought...

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.830
I told them not to say anything.

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.630
You should have told me then.

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:51.920
There was nothing I could do back then.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.180
I never even dreamed that Joonsang would come back to life.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.800
Fate brought us back together.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.730
I love you, Minhyung.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.740
Thank you for going out of your way to come here.

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.000
Have you forgotten that he's my patient?

00:02:48.370 --> 00:02:50.150
I was hoping we could do this

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:53.250
at the cabin I used to visit when your father was still alive.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:55.130
Would that be all right?

00:02:55.710 --> 00:02:56.960
As you wish.

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.090
I'll let Deputy Manager Kim know.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.770
Will Minhyung be all right?

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.140
We'll have to give it some time.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.810
You may want to prepare yourself for the worst.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.110
Excuse me?

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:20.820
Joonsang will want to recover his lost self.

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.070
Anything but that, Doctor—

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.830
Don't make the same mistake twice.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.040
Please, Doctor.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.080
Please use that hypnosis you mentioned

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.880
to erase the memories that are tormenting him.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.170
Please, I beg of you.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:37.840
I understand it's hard,

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:41.090
but these things take time.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.840
Let's see how things play out over time.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:44.810
Just do it.

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:45.550
Just do it now.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:47.850
No matter how painful a memory may be,

00:03:48.510 --> 00:03:51.180
those memories are what have pieced together his present.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.190
Just give him new memories then.

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:56.800
Just give him memories of the father he so desperately wanted.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:58.190
Please, Doctor!

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:02.860
If you forcibly replace his memories like that,

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.200
he may lose something even more important in the future.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.700
I'll take full responsibility.

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:12.750
This isn't something you can be responsible for;

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.750
this is Joonsang's life, not yours.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:15.690
He's my son.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:16.630
It's my...

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:18.710
choice.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.220
Let Joonsang decide for himself.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.890
That's the right choice here.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:58.000
Joonsang.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:35.870
Don't you hate Dad sometimes, Mom?

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.790
Why would I hate him?

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.500
This may sound strange to you,

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:44.420
but I still feel nothing but gratitude towards him.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:50.640
Even when you're the only one still loving and missing him now?

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:54.040
Even when the sad and painful moments

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:57.440
far outweigh the happy times you've had with him, like now?

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.440
Yujin.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:04.440
These things can't be forgotten no matter how much time goes by.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.610
Once you've engraved someone in your heart, he's there forever.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.110
Excuse me?

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:05.540
Are you all right?

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.050
What high school did you graduate from?

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.550
Was it in America?

00:07:10.050 --> 00:07:12.760
Have you heard of Chuncheon?

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:15.890
Don't you remember Jeil High School in Chuncheon?

00:07:16.140 --> 00:07:18.560
Are you sure you've never lived in Korea before?

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.940
Could you take off your glasses for a minute?

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.080
Minhyung?

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.560
You guys should get married soon.

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.400
I already started working on Yujin's wedding dress;

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:07.610
it should be done soon.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.820
You and Yujin will both like it, I'm sure.

00:08:11.990 --> 00:08:15.110
Did something happen between you and Mr. Minhyung?

00:08:15.990 --> 00:08:17.620
No.

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:19.580
Just marry Yujin quickly, okay?

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:24.460
Why are you saying this all of a sudden?

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:26.710
You love Yujin, right?

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:29.500
Am I right?

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:32.760
Mr. Minhyung's...

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.220
What about him?

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:38.520
Nothing.

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:39.990
I was just going to say that we were going to get married soon

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.270
without you telling us.

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:41.890
Really?

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:43.980
Yeah, thanks for worrying.

00:08:44.140 --> 00:08:47.520
I'm sure Yujin will be happy to hear about her wedding dress.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:49.650
Producer Kim?

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:51.940
I'm gonna get going.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:52.820
See you.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:55.710
Thanks, Chelin.

00:08:55.710 --> 00:08:57.410
I'll be looking forward to the wedding dress.

00:08:57.910 --> 00:08:58.380
Yeah.

00:08:58.380 --> 00:08:59.140
See you.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.030
Bye.

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.690
Look who it is.

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:37.530
I wouldn't have recognized you, if the Doctor

00:09:37.530 --> 00:09:39.200
hadn't told me you were coming.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:40.200
Do you remember me?

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:41.660
You're the man who...

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:43.200
Looks like you do.

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:44.660
When I was little...

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.000
That's right.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:49.000
When you were little, I saved you here.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.040
Thank you so much.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:57.050
Oh no, it's not like I did it because I wanted you all to thank me;

00:09:57.380 --> 00:10:00.640
but your mother keeps thanking me every time she sees me,

00:10:00.760 --> 00:10:02.720
so it's embarrassing the hell out of me.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.020
Aren't you gentlemen hungry?

00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:07.390
I'm about to die of hunger.

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:11.980
Oh, you're here, Doctor.

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:14.570
How would you like some trout sashimi for lunch?

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:16.030
Sounds good.

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:17.070
Is that all right with you?

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.330
I'm relieved to hear that he's with you, Doctor.

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.330
I'll leave him in your care.

00:10:30.420 --> 00:10:31.630
I'll go with this one.

00:10:32.960 --> 00:10:34.380
Try not to make a big deal about this.

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.800
This is your first concert in Korea in ten years.

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:40.220
I think it'll be hard for the press not to make a big deal about it.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:43.220
I'm just asking you to make sure things don't get out of hand.

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:45.930
Just say "no" to any interview requests.

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:47.940
You're going back to Seoul today, aren't you?

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.440
Should I get a piano ready so you can practice right away?

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:53.230
There's somewhere I need to visit before that.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:03.600
Please, Doctor.

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.490
I want to recover my lost memories.

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.700
Joonsang was unhappy.

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:09.710
He denied his past

00:11:09.710 --> 00:11:12.080
because of all the memories he didn't want to remember.

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:15.840
Knowing that, what makes you want to get them back?

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:20.550
Have you ever had to wait for a delayed train?

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.590
Someone might still be out there, waiting for Joonsang.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.310
But ten years...

00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:29.140
it's a long time to wait.

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:33.730
Even more so if that someone had actually spent it waiting.

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:37.940
When you gain something you're bound to lose something as well.

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:40.530
Things might get all tangled up and confusing,

00:11:40.530 --> 00:11:43.110
whether you want them to or not.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.820
Whether I wanted to do it or not never mattered in the first place, anyway.

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:56.290
Do you think you can handle it?

00:11:56.790 --> 00:12:00.840
A train can stop at designated stations, but a person's heart can not.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:04.930
I want to find out.

00:12:13.690 --> 00:12:16.360
I came alone today, Daddy.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:19.070
You already figured out that I've got something on my mind, huh?

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.760
<i>I think we both need some time to think this over.</i>

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:46.300
<i>If you still want to go ahead with it after thinking it through,</i>

00:12:46.890 --> 00:12:48.890
<i>I'll help you then.</i>

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:56.550
Christmas is only a week away,

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.190
and I'm sure you're all dying for it to arrive.

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:00.000
I hope you'll also be looking forward

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:02.670
to the live Christmas concert we're holding

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:04.490
for all you listeners out there.

00:13:04.900 --> 00:13:09.200
We're going to end today's show with a song that's full of Christmas spirit;

00:13:09.620 --> 00:13:12.790
please enjoy, "First Christmas."

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:33.920
Hello?

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:35.310
Oh hi, Huijin.

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:39.940
I'm still in Chuncheon, why?

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:46.140
Right now?

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:47.530
Why at the school?

00:13:48.250 --> 00:13:48.850
Yeah.

00:13:53.760 --> 00:13:54.430
Yes.

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:56.370
I understand.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.290
I'll call you back.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:02.130
No good?

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:08.380
So this is what it feels like to be rejected by your first love.

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:09.550
Your first love?

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:13.310
Didn't I tell you that Mi Hee Kang was my first love?

00:14:13.850 --> 00:14:16.020
I stopped playing piano at an early age,

00:14:16.140 --> 00:14:19.160
but she inspired me to keep listening to classical music

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:21.060
and even do a classical radio show.

00:14:21.810 --> 00:14:23.940
I'll see what I can do.

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.320
Do you have some connections or something?

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.070
But in return, I have a favor I want to ask of you as well...

00:14:39.330 --> 00:14:41.650
Why do you want to change the venue

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:44.170
when we're only days away from the concert?

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:49.630
Isn't it a reasonable idea to hold a Christmas concert on a field of snow?

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.830
Whose idea was it?

00:14:51.830 --> 00:14:52.890
Tell me.

00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:54.050
Was it yours?

00:14:54.510 --> 00:14:55.720
It was me.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.140
It was my idea.

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.520
The production costs for this will be through the roof.

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:03.270
Does it have to be this specific resort, Producer Kim?

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:04.190
Yes.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.820
But why here?

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:08.860
Because my fiancée is there now.

00:15:12.450 --> 00:15:17.080
This is the only way I'll get to spend Christmas with her this year.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:20.870
This man's...

00:15:21.040 --> 00:15:21.960
Please.

00:15:30.630 --> 00:15:31.990
Fine.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:32.720
Go for it.

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:37.430
Thank you so much.

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:38.560
Thank you.

00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:36.670
<i>Don't fall asleep, Joonsang!</i>

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:46.640
What's your name?

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:51.190
My name is...

00:17:56.400 --> 00:17:57.110
My name is...

00:17:58.150 --> 00:18:00.700
<i>Don't fall asleep, Joonsang!</i>

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.630
<i>You're really going to get it if you don't show up</i>

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:08.100
<i>to today's lunch broadcast too.</i>

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.830
<i>Thanks for helping me climb over the fence.</i>

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:17.050
<i>This is the first time I've sent someone a paper note in class.</i>

00:18:17.220 --> 00:18:18.170
<i>Be thankful.</i>

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.390
<i>What are you doing over winter break?</i>

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:24.600
<i>Why don't we discuss it over a pastry today?</i>

00:18:24.890 --> 00:18:26.060
<i>You're buying of course.</i>

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:01.380
<i>Here's your Christmas present, Yujin.</i>

00:19:04.550 --> 00:19:06.100
<i>Nah, that's not it.</i>

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:13.560
<i>I present to you "The First Time"; the song you like so much, Yujin.</i>

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:18.650
<i>I know it's late, but I got you a Christmas present.</i>

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:22.860
<i>That's still kind of awkward.</i>

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:48.760
That's why you called me here, Huijin?

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:49.400
Yeah, and I call it:

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:52.220
"Operation Wish Gargamel a Happy Birthday

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:54.440
by Moving His Heart and Making Him Cry."

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:56.940
What the heck?

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:04.660
I just can't figure out what might move Gargamel though.

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:08.240
And that's where my smarts come in, right?

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:09.740
Please, Yujin?

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:14.420
All right, I'll tell you.

00:20:14.670 --> 00:20:16.040
Yay!

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:19.590
Gargamel, I mean Mr. Park,

00:20:19.710 --> 00:20:22.470
has a soft side for romantic poems.

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:24.010
No way.

00:20:24.430 --> 00:20:25.260
Get outta here.

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:26.760
Then what can we do?

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:28.680
Are you sure?

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:29.510
Yeah.

00:20:29.640 --> 00:20:34.520
He cried us a river the last time we read him a romantic poem.

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:37.270
Why don't you give it a shot, Huijin?

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:37.940
Me?

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:39.070
Here.

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:41.230
Yeah, go for it, Huijin.

00:20:41.360 --> 00:20:42.820
Come on.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:46.610
Give it a shot.

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:21.150
<i>Turn around with your longing eyes</i>

00:21:22.400 --> 00:21:25.190
<i>and see me following you.</i>

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:31.370
<i>Raise me up with your love.</i>

00:21:33.040 --> 00:21:36.080
<i>Just like how the gentle breeze keeps the swallow afloat,</i>

00:21:37.370 --> 00:21:41.090
<i>whether it be sunny or storming,</i>

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:47.510
<i>keep us afloat, so that we may be able to fly far away.</i>

00:21:49.260 --> 00:21:52.720
<i>But what should I do</i>

00:21:53.510 --> 00:21:57.560
<i>when first love calls on me again?</i>

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:24.040
Didn't you say you couldn't play piano?

00:22:24.960 --> 00:22:26.460
I never said that.

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:44.150
<i>Hold me tight,</i>

00:22:45.320 --> 00:22:49.070
<i>like the magnificent seas embracing the waves.</i>

00:22:49.820 --> 00:22:55.870
<i>Take me back to your hidden house inside the mountains.</i>

00:22:56.740 --> 00:22:58.080
Mr. Park!

00:22:59.000 --> 00:23:00.040
What is it?

00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:04.000
Happy Birthday!

00:23:08.170 --> 00:23:09.880
Why you punks.

00:23:13.260 --> 00:23:16.240
<i>Take me back to your hidden house</i>

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:18.810
<i>inside the mountains;</i>

00:23:20.770 --> 00:23:23.020
<i>to the house where the roof is thatched with happiness</i>

00:23:23.940 --> 00:23:28.190
<i>and the door is made of love.</i>

00:23:29.240 --> 00:23:32.280
<i>But what should I do</i>

00:23:32.860 --> 00:23:36.700
<i>when first love calls on me again?</i>
